  "method": {
    "scale": "Every indicator is scored 1 (low) to 5 (severe). A category score is the average of its indicators. The PREVENT structural index is the average of the six structural categories (P, R, E, V, E, N). Triggers (T) are listed as flags and never averaged in, because the framework locates the risk in how those in power respond to them.",
    "auto": "World Bank and V-Dem (via Our World in Data) indicators refresh daily; UCDP conflict events refresh monthly once a UCDP token is configured. Each is scored against thresholds stored in data/prevent.json. Neighbouring violence counts UCDP deaths in other countries within about 200 km of approximate border points; until UCDP data is available it falls back to the highest Lab conflict score among ASEAN neighbours.",
    "adaptation": "Adapted by Scarecrow from the AIPG PREVENT Risk Assessment Framework. The framework does not prescribe scales, weights or thresholds; these are Scarecrow's choices.",
    "review": "Exception-based review: an automated score that moves by more than one step from the last published score is held, and the previous score stays public until the Lab approves the change in the Review Room. Upcoming elections recorded by the Lab appear automatically as triggers from 180 days before to 30 days after the vote."
  },
